{
  "id": "c-cadence-orcad-task-08-windows",
  "snapshot": "OrCAD24.1",
  "instruction": "`C:\\Users\\user\\Desktop\\TUTOR2.DSN` is a schematic. Traverse all primitive part instances in it and export `C:\\Users\\user\\Desktop\\pin_map.json`. The top-level JSON fields must be `total_parts`, `total_pins`, and `parts`. The `parts` array must be sorted ascending by `ref`, and each element must have the form `{ref, pin_count, pin_numbers}`. Requirements: - Multipart instances that share the same refdes must be merged into one entry. - `pin_numbers` must be merged, deduplicated, and sorted lexicographically. - `total_parts` must equal the length of the `parts` array. - `total_pins` must equal the sum of all `pin_count` values. [Software] Use OrCAD's native Capture design converter `C:\\Cadence\\SPB_24.1\\tools\\bin\\cap2xml.exe`. At the start of the task, use `C:\\Cadence\\SPB_24.1\\tools\\bin\\Capture.exe` for OrCAD schematics and `C:\\Cadence\\SPB_24.1\\tools\\bin\\allegro.exe` for board work.",
